title: TutorialManager
---
<<lock>>
PHYLL: Hiya Lily, how's your first day goin'?
-> Good . . .
-> No one's come to this counter yet.
PHYLL: Yeah, pretty slow business so far.
PHYLL: But the freaks in this part of town always start showing up around this time.
PHYLL: No doubt they'll come over for a quick pick-me-up after the show!
PHYLL: In the meantime, why don't you show me what you learned in that fancy magic school of yours?
<<setInternal>>
He's talking about Barvard University of Thaumaturgy and Transmutation, which you totally lied about on your resume.
The only alchemic experience you have is a 20 dollar online witchery course, taught by Madame Legrange of Nevada.
<<setNormal>>
PHYLL: I'm preparing for a long shift, and I gotta pick up my boyfriend after he's done with his affair.
PHYLL: So I could really use a potion to wake me up!
PHYLL: Since you're new here, a few reminders…
PHYLL: You can use your noggin to CHECK characters, ingredients, and potions to learn more about them.
PHYLL: If you're observant, you might be able to find an even bigger problem to solve for your customers!
PHYLL: Why don't you try CHECKing me? (HINT: Press 'Q' on my SPRITE!)
<<unlock>>
<<stop>>
===

title: TutorialManager_PostCheck
---
<<lock>>
PHYLL: Our equipment is a bit peculiar...
PHYLL: ... so you'll need to mash your ingredients in the mortar and pestle before mixing them in the cauldron.
PHYLL: Why don't you start with a Ratwurst, by the cash register?
<<unlock>>
<<stop>>
===

title: TutorialManager_PostRatwurst
---
<<lock>>
PHYLL: Great! I'm sure a Barvard grad already knows this…
PHYLL: But you need 3 mashed ingredients in the cauldron to make yourself a potion.
PHYLL: You can FOCUS on the mortar and the cauldron by pressing 'E' on them.
PHYLL: When you're all done, press 'E' again to zoom out.
PHYLL: Alrighty! I'll leave the rest up to you. Happy brewing!
<<unlock>>
<<stop>>
===

title: TutorialManager_Ending
---
<<setNormal>>
<<if $potion_quality == "arousal">>
<<setsprite "Phyll" "manager sad">>
    PHYLL: What's… this feeling??
    PHYLL: Urghh… my head…
    PHYLL: All I can think about is… elf abs… and elf arrows…
    PHYLL: Long, piercing, elf arrows…
<<setsprite "Phyll" "manager happy">>
    PHYLL: LILY!! I GOTTA GO FIND MY BOYFRIEND.
    PHYLL: YOU'RE IN CHARGE WHILE I'M GONE.
    PHYLL: DON'T CALL ME. DON'T TEXT ME. I'LL BE BUSY.
    PHYLL: I'M COMING POOKIEEEEEEEE
    ...
    I think that went well.
    <<loadGameplay>>
<<elseif $potion_quality == "wakefulness">>
<<setsprite "Phyll" "manager happy">>
    PHYLL: This was exactly what I was looking for! Wow, you're a natural!
    PHYLL: Thanks Lily! Now I'll be able to stay awake on the drive home. My boyfriend will be thrilled.
    PHYLL: I'll leave you to it, then. If you need anything, I'll be in the back.
    <<loadGameplay>>
<<else>>
<<setsprite "Phyll" "manager sad">>
    PHYLL: Hm, this isn't exactly what I'm looking for…
    PHYLL: Good effort anyway, Lily! 
    PHYLL: I'm sure there are some limitations with our ingredients that your Barvard-educated brain isn't used to.
    PHYLL: I'll leave you to it, then. If you need anything, I'll be in the back.
    <<loadGameplay>>
<<endif>>
===

title: TutorialManager_Check
---
<<setInternal>>
It's Phyll Kloro. My favorite manager. Yup.
He's actually pretty chill for being 142 years old.
I guess that's only 28 in Treeple years.
I heard he actually graduated top of his class in Botanical Rights, but he's been working here for the past few years.
It's tough out here, but he's always got a pretty good attitude. I like that about him.
Anyway, Phyll somehow has the HOTTEST elf boyfriend I've ever seen.
I mean, Treeples reproduce through pollination, so they don't really… have sex? Or have much libido at all.
So interracial relationships tend to be pretty rare for Treeple.
And Phyll's solution to this problem… is letting his boyfriend have all the affairs he wants.
He plays it cool, but I can tell it bothers him. To reiterate, his boyfriend is SERIOUSLY hot.
Wonder if I can do anything to help him out…
<<setNormal>>
<<jump TutorialManager_PostCheck>>
<<stop>>
===

title: TutorialManager_GivePotion
---
<<lock>>
<<setInternal>>
-> Give Potion
    <<confirmGive>>
    <<jump TutorialManager_Ending>>
-> Don't Give
    <<cancelGive>>
<<unlock>>
<<stop>>
===